1️⃣ Stop & Remove All Containers

docker stop $(docker ps -aq)  
docker rm $(docker ps -aq)
2️⃣ Remove All Docker Images

docker rmi $(docker images -q) -f
3️⃣ Remove All Docker Networks

docker network prune -f
4️⃣ Remove All Docker Volumes

docker volume prune -f
5️⃣ Verify Everything is Clean

docker ps -a   # No containers should be listed
docker images  # No images should be listed
docker network ls  # Only default networks should remain
docker volume ls  # No volumes should be listed
🚀 Now your Docker environment is completely clean! Let me know if you need further assistance.
